/-!
# Inductive limits of C⋆-algebras

Let `(A i, f i j)` be a directed system of (possibly nonunital) complex C⋆-algebras indexed by a
directed preorder `ι`, with `⋆`-algebra homomorphisms `f i j hij : A i → A j` as transition maps.
The transition maps need not be injective: because every `⋆`-homomorphism between C⋆-algebras is
contractive (`NonUnitalStarAlgHom.norm_apply_le`), the net
`j ↦ ‖f i j.1 (Set.mem_Ici.mp j.2) x‖` on the upper ray `Set.Ici i` is antitone and bounded below
by `0`, so its limit and infimum agree and define an asymptotic C⋆-seminorm `stageSeminorm A f i`
on each stage `A i`.

Invariance along transitions descends `stageSeminorm` to the algebraic colimit `DirectLimit A f` on
the type synonym `SeminormedDirectLimit A f`, making it a seminormed `⋆`-algebra satisfying the
C⋆-identity `‖star z * z‖ = ‖z‖ * ‖z‖`. Its separated Hausdorff completion
(`UniformSpace.Completion`, which simultaneously quotients out the null ideal `{z | ‖z‖ = 0}` and
completes in norm) is the *C⋆-inductive limit* `TauCeti.CStarInductiveLimit A f`. When the stages
are unital C⋆-algebras and the transition maps preserve the unit, the same type carries a canonical
`CStarAlgebra` structure extending its `NonUnitalCStarAlgebra` structure definitionally.

Every compatible family of `⋆`-homomorphisms `g i : A i →⋆ₙₐ[ℂ] B` into a C⋆-algebra `B` is
automatically bounded by `stageSeminorm` (since `‖g i x‖ = ‖g j (f i j hij x)‖ ≤ ‖f i j hij x‖`
for all `j ≥ i`), and therefore extends uniquely to a `⋆`-homomorphism
`CStarInductiveLimit.lift A f g hg : CStarInductiveLimit A f →⋆ₙₐ[ℂ] B` without any auxiliary norm
hypothesis. Its range is `closure (⋃ i, Set.range (g i))`, and it is injective if and only if
`‖g i x‖ = stageSeminorm A f i x` for all `i` and `x`; this yields the recognition theorem
identifying `CStarInductiveLimit A f` with any ambient C⋆-algebra generated by a compatible family
satisfying the asymptotic norm formula (in particular, any increasing union of C⋆-subalgebras).

Closed two-sided ideals and preservation of C⋆-simplicity under inductive limits are developed in
`TauCeti.Analysis.CStarAlgebra.InductiveLimit.Ideal`.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.CStarInductiveLimit.stageSeminorm`: the asymptotic C⋆-seminorm
  `x ↦ ⨅ j : Set.Ici i, ‖f i j.1 (Set.mem_Ici.mp j.2) x‖` on stage `A i`.
* `TauCeti.CStarInductiveLimit.SeminormedDirectLimit`: the algebraic direct limit `DirectLimit A f`
  carrying the descended asymptotic C⋆-seminorm.
* `TauCeti.CStarInductiveLimit`: the C⋆-inductive limit of `(A i, f i j)`, equipped with
  `NonUnitalCStarAlgebra`, `NonUnitalCommCStarAlgebra`, `CStarAlgebra`, and `CommCStarAlgebra`
  instances as appropriate.
* `TauCeti.CStarInductiveLimit.fromDirectLimit`, `TauCeti.CStarInductiveLimit.of`,
  `TauCeti.CStarInductiveLimit.fromDirectLimitUnital`, and `TauCeti.CStarInductiveLimit.ofUnital`:
  canonical `⋆`-homomorphisms from `DirectLimit A f` and stages `A i`.
* `TauCeti.CStarInductiveLimit.lift`, `TauCeti.CStarInductiveLimit.liftEquiv`,
  `TauCeti.CStarInductiveLimit.liftUnital`, and `TauCeti.CStarInductiveLimit.liftUnitalEquiv`:
  universal properties in the categories of nonunital and unital C⋆-algebras.
* `TauCeti.CStarInductiveLimit.equivOfDenseUnion` and
  `TauCeti.CStarInductiveLimit.equivOfInjectiveDenseUnion`: uniqueness and recognition of
  C⋆-inductive limits inside an ambient C⋆-algebra.
* `TauCeti.CStarInductiveLimit.map`, `TauCeti.CStarInductiveLimit.mapUnital`,
  `TauCeti.CStarInductiveLimit.mapEquiv`, and `TauCeti.CStarInductiveLimit.equivOfIsTop`:
  functoriality and stabilization at a top index.

## Main statements

* `TauCeti.CStarInductiveLimit.norm_of`, `TauCeti.CStarInductiveLimit.norm_of_lt_iff`, and
  `TauCeti.CStarInductiveLimit.tendsto_norm_atTop_norm_of`:
  `‖of A f i x‖ = ⨅ j : Set.Ici i, ‖f i j.1 (Set.mem_Ici.mp j.2) x‖ = lim_j ‖f i j hij x‖`.
* `TauCeti.CStarInductiveLimit.mem_ker_of_iff`: `x ∈ ker (of A f i)` iff `‖f i j hij x‖ → 0`.
* `TauCeti.CStarInductiveLimit.isometry_of` and `TauCeti.CStarInductiveLimit.of_injective`:
  `of A f i` is isometric whenever transitions out of `i` are injective.
* `TauCeti.CStarInductiveLimit.dense_iUnion_range_of` and
  `TauCeti.CStarInductiveLimit.exists_finset_norm_sub_of_lt`: density of the union of stage images
  and simultaneous approximation of finite subsets at a common stage.
* `TauCeti.CStarInductiveLimit.range_lift` and `TauCeti.CStarInductiveLimit.lift_injective_iff`:
  range and injectivity of universally lifted `⋆`-homomorphisms.
* `TauCeti.CStarInductiveLimit.instSeparableSpace`: countable inductive limits of separable
  C⋆-algebras are separable.

## References

* Bruce Blackadar, *Operator Algebras: Theory of C*-Algebras and von Neumann Algebras*,
  Section II.8.2 (II.8.2.1–II.8.2.2, II.8.2.4).
* Gerard J. Murphy, *C*-Algebras and Operator Theory*, Section 6.1.
* Kenneth R. Davidson, *C*-Algebras by Example*, Section III.1.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

open Filter Topology UniformSpace
